WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:30.000
The

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.320
begins at page 63.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:36.540
All right?

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:40.440
But actually,

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.240
the theme of the perasha,

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:43.880
to understand what's going on in the perasha,

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:47.040
you must go to the

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.300
end of last perasha,

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:49.880
leplecha,

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:51.640
page 60,

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:55.640
verse 24.

00:00:57.880 --> 00:00:59.340
And there you read,

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.340
that

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:03.740
Abraham

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:03.900
that Abraham

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:14.460
that Abraham was 99 years old

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:17.660
when he circumcised himself

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:20.500
the last paschal

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:32.220
And all his household, including his slaves,

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:35.020
the circumcised themselves with him.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:38.480
But now I come to the point.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:44.460
It means that they were circumcised because of him.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:46.580
Now one minute.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:50.220
One of the most traumatic experiences

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:52.420
in the life of Abraham

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:56.320
was when at the age of 99

00:01:56.320 --> 00:02:00.720
he had to circumcise himself.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:03.100
As a matter of fact,

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:05.140
the trauma was so profound

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:08.920
that we mention it every day in the tefillah.

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:10.940
You know in the salam we say

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:12.600
about the guy,

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:14.600
وَإِخَارُتْ عَنْ مُوْهَا بَرِيدٍ

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.260
What does it mean,

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:17.440
وَإِخَارُتْ عَنْ مُوْهَا بَرِيدٍ?

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:18.540
It means,

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:21.600
as the haqqani say that it was so difficult

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.920
for Abraham to circumcise

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:25.680
himself that Bari'ulam

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:26.620
took him

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.880
with the arm, took his arm

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:31.420
and together God and Abraham

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:33.020
the kharot and moab

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:35.900
God had to hold his arm

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:37.100
so to speak steady

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:39.720
alright, and so that

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:41.780
he was able to circumcise

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:43.680
himself, and now we understand

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:44.860
the last pasuk said

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:47.920
when they saw this act of Abraham

00:02:47.920 --> 00:03:04.560
everybody, so this kind of action, they circumcise themselves with it. That's the end of the

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:13.120
parasha today. Next parasha, it begins at the third line of the milah, three days later.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.380
Chachamim tells

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:17.500
that the third day of the Milah

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:19.600
is the most painful of all the days

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:21.960
that was a very

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:23.020
hot day

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:24.920
it was in the summer

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:28.000
probably around the month of July

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:29.920
and he was

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:31.780
in one of the hottest places

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:32.700
in the world

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:34.960
Elon Moreh

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:38.080
that was one of the hottest places in the world

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:39.680
and now

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:40.480
he is

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:43.360
in a tent

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:45.640
is so hot

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:47.980
that he cannot be inside the tent

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:50.280
because it's too hot inside the tent.

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:52.200
He cannot be outside the tent

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:52.940
but he is

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:56.160
he is by the entrance.

00:03:56.860 --> 00:03:58.540
And you know why he is by the entrance?

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:01.460
Because the day is so hot.

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:03.020
He cannot be inside.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:06.040
He cannot be outside.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:08.460
He is right by the door.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:09.400
Yes?

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:11.820
And something happened.

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.720
Now, I want you to enter, to penetrate

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:17.300
the mind of Abraham Avinu.

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:19.440
99 years old,

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:22.040
just circumcised himself

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:25.040
in enormous amount of pain.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:27.220
He is weak.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:30.760
He has nobody.

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:33.380
God promised him the world.

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:35.520
But in point of fact, what does he have?

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:38.060
A tent in the middle of the desert.

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:40.940
no son, no Isaac yet

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:41.720
alright

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:45.180
Sarah was supposed to be the mother of many children

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:46.920
she is a 90

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:48.800
years old lady, alright

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:49.940
no hope

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:50.840
alright

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:54.440
he did what people would say

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:56.040
one of the craziest things in the world

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:58.200
yes, circumcise yourself

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:01.160
now he is in that situation

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:04.220
vayyera elav

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:05.740
adonai belone

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:06.460
mamre

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:09.900
and at the third day

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:12.180
during this mode of anguish

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:13.860
self-examination

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:15.360
God

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:18.060
vayyera elav adonai belone mamre

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:20.560
God revealed himself to Abraham

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:22.340
belone mamre

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:23.660
in the valley of mamre

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:24.820
where this happened

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:28.200
where who?

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:29.040
in Abraham

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:36.180
your shepherd Petah Ha'ohel. He is at the entrance and he is not inside, he is not

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:43.980
outside, he is Petah Ha'ohel, as the day was getting hotter and hotter.

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:51.420
He knows that he has a vision. He saw enough. He raises his eyes, and he sees something.

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:56.140
Now I want you to picture the situation. He's down in the valley, Elonim Amrev,

00:05:56.140 --> 00:06:05.780
he is in a valley, he raises his eyes, and there is a road, and on the road, above his head,

00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:14.300
above the horizon, yes, he sees the initial Osham HaNashim, the three men, Nusabim Ala,

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:22.420
they are standing up on the road, he is down in the valley, and they are standing, Nusabim Ala,

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:23.500
on top of them.

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:25.500
Vajab.

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:28.200
And as soon as he sees it,

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:29.780
Vajab

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:33.220
he runs

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:34.580
from

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:36.380
the entrance of the oil

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:38.360
Vajab to meet them.

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:40.420
I want you to understand

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:41.560
the situation very well.

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:43.960
He's sitting down here below

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:45.520
above

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:47.540
maybe 20, 30

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:49.580
yards above.

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:52.320
He sees three men standing on top of

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:53.940
him, and then the man

00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:55.720
continued on the road.

00:06:56.820 --> 00:06:57.260
And then,

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:00.280
he goes to run to meet

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:01.800
them. He knows that if he would run

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:03.120
upwards this way,

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:05.800
he's not going to be able to reach them.

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:07.640
So he goes diagonally,

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:11.460
I'm not going to be able to meet them.

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:13.500
Once again.

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:15.580
What happened

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:16.680
to the old man?

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:18.320
To the brave man?

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:20.920
To the man that was totally exhausted?

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:22.700
how this old man

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:23.920
can run

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:25.260
what happened

00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:29.880
he wasn't

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:30.740
how did he know

00:07:30.740 --> 00:07:34.340
that he was hurting

00:07:34.340 --> 00:07:35.300
he was hurting

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:38.860
that is the visit of God

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:43.360
as he made circumcision

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:45.980
a metamorphosis

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:48.160
took place in the body

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:49.300
of Abraham Abinu

00:07:49.300 --> 00:08:08.480
He changed. He is no longer old. He could run so fast that not only he could climb the upward elevation, but moreover he is able to catch up with the travelers.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:10.720
v'yaros nikatan

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:12.720
and he did this

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:13.840
m'petah ha'ohel

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:16.560
he didn't have to walk a few steps and then run

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:18.300
m'petah ha'ohel

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:20.680
he sprang like a runner

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:23.120
m'petah ha'ohel

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:24.720
v'yaros nikatan

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:25.640
m'petah ha'ohel

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:29.100
now you understand the transformation in the body of Abraham

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:30.420
a miracle

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:32.420
it's the miracle of circumcision

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:35.100
it's the miracle of rejuvenation

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:36.560
a new birth

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:37.500
yes

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:39.460
and that's the

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:41.520
image that we have here, right?

00:08:42.340 --> 00:08:43.320
وَيَارُزِكْ

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:45.460
قَتَامْ بِدَابْ وَإِشْتَحُوا

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:47.440
آرْسًا, and when he sees them

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:49.100
he bowed down to them

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:51.480
now one of the

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:52.180
great

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:55.640
discoveries of Abraham

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:57.460
was that he discovered

00:08:57.460 --> 00:08:58.640
the unity of God

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:01.540
that's great, discovered

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:03.620
that there is a God in the universe, creator, etc

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:04.560
that's great

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:07.300
but people do not understand

00:09:07.300 --> 00:09:10.700
what we mean by knowing that there is a God.

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:13.840
If there is a God in the universe,

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:19.280
and if every individual is created

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:21.360
Beselem Elohim in the image of God,

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:24.980
this belief should be translated

00:09:24.980 --> 00:09:27.720
in a certain kind of relationship,

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:30.060
attitude towards fellow humans.

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:34.120
The great discovery of Abraham Avinu

00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:35.640
was not only that there is a God,

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:37.660
but because there is a God

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:38.880
our relationship

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:41.540
should be different

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:43.380
and you see it here

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:45.440
in the Misbah that he instituted

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:47.640
he invented a Misbah

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:50.000
the Misbah of Akhenasat Orhim

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:51.920
that you see a poor

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:53.640
wayfarer, yes

00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:54.940
traveling in the desert

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:58.040
you don't know him, you never saw him before

00:09:58.040 --> 00:09:59.420
you will never see him again

00:09:59.420 --> 00:10:01.260
that you do something

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:03.360
that is part of the Hebrew

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:05.460
mentality today, thanks to Abraham

00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:06.580
and give me a lot of chastity.

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:09.780
You do something for the sake of goodness.

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:11.940
And then when he meets them,

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:13.300
he says, hey you,

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:14.980
would you like to have a glass of water?

00:10:15.740 --> 00:10:18.840
He bows down to them.

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:20.720
He greets them.

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:23.800
The notion of treating the stranger

00:10:23.800 --> 00:10:25.660
not as an enemy,

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:29.960
but as somebody whom you respect.

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:31.820
Treating somebody with respect.

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:35.260
Normally, when we bring a fool into our home,

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:40.600
If we bring a poor into our home, we treat this person sometimes with deference,

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:43.060
and sometimes with not, not with deference.

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:45.840
Sometimes we treat them like second class, and so on.

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:49.200
What's the importance here of Abraham Avinu was teaching us,

00:10:49.340 --> 00:10:52.760
that's why we became such a powerful people, such an extraordinary people,

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:53.140
is,

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:58.400
you respect your fellow men.

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:00.200
You respect other people.

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:02.220
All right?

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:04.880
and now he speaks to them and says

00:11:04.880 --> 00:11:05.620
by your mouth

00:11:05.620 --> 00:11:08.240
Adonai, my Lord

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:13.560
if I find grace in your eyes

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:18.440
he addresses himself to the oldest person and says

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:19.740
do not pass me by

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:21.540
now here again

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:24.240
normally you will ask

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:26.320
I mean the poor person will ask

00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:28.000
the wealthy person

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:30.360
may I have something from you

00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:31.740
would you do me a favor

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:34.140
and give me a glass of water

00:11:34.140 --> 00:11:36.240
which will be to my favor and let me

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:37.860
stay by the shade of your tree.

00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:40.360
In the case of Abraham Avinu,

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:41.840
he has then

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:44.640
divested to him a favor.

00:11:45.340 --> 00:11:46.600
And from here the Chachabim says,

00:11:46.980 --> 00:11:48.600
Gadol is greater

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:50.220
the favor that the Oreh

00:11:50.220 --> 00:11:51.980
makes to the Baal Abai

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:53.780
than what the Baal Abai makes to the Oreh.

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:56.180
Or, in other words,

00:11:56.340 --> 00:11:58.740
is greater the favor that the poor makes to the rich

00:11:58.740 --> 00:12:00.500
than what the rich does

00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:01.040
to the poor.

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:03.540
That's the whole idea. It's not only charity.

00:12:03.640 --> 00:12:05.080
It's not charity in the vulgar

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:07.400
Western Christian

00:12:07.400 --> 00:12:08.940
sense, you know, with

00:12:08.940 --> 00:12:10.720
patronizing somebody.

00:12:11.240 --> 00:12:12.620
In Navasad, he

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:13.680
henve'en echa.

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:16.440
Al nata aborme al abdecha.

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:19.120
Please, would you let me

00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:21.040
invite you to my

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:22.160
home, alright?

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:26.380
And now he says,

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:29.240
I'm going to give you

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:30.420
a little bit of water.

00:12:30.420 --> 00:12:40.200
and rest under the tree.

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:42.960
Now, one of the

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:45.400
earmarks of the sattik

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:47.040
is the haqqani say,

00:12:47.140 --> 00:12:48.640
sattik, omer me'at

00:12:48.640 --> 00:12:49.980
ve'osey harve.

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:52.680
Rishayim, omerim harve

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:54.140
ve'osey shumdabad.

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:56.240
You know, that's the point, that's what the haqqani say.

00:12:56.240 --> 00:12:57.900
Here, what he said,

00:12:57.900 --> 00:13:04.400
I'm not going to give you much, just let me give you a little bit of water.

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:06.260
And rest in the retreat.

00:13:07.060 --> 00:13:07.280
Alright?

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:10.580
In that case, he's going to do much more.

00:13:11.380 --> 00:13:13.600
Now, the kapha training.

00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:16.920
I'm going to give you a loaf of bread.

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:19.660
You strengthen with food.

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:23.080
You nourish your heart.

00:13:24.300 --> 00:13:27.560
And then you continue on your journey.

00:13:27.900 --> 00:13:44.560
Do what you said.

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:45.680
Now,

00:13:46.980 --> 00:13:48.460
Abraham is no longer old,

00:13:49.060 --> 00:13:50.560
he's no longer 99 years old,

00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:52.640
he's no longer a just circumcised person,

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:54.360
he's a young man.

00:13:54.360 --> 00:13:59.160
by Mahir Abraham, and Abraham rushes

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:03.120
to the tent of Salam.

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:06.120
He goes to the tent of Salam.

00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:11.120
The great Akhla Rahim is a partnership between husband and wife.

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:14.120
The husband cannot do it by himself, the wife cannot do it by herself.

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:18.120
It's a partnership. And here we have the first case in history

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:21.120
of Akhla Rahim we have it here.

